3057. Employees Project Allocation
Table: Project
Column Name	Type
project_id	int
employee_id	int
workload	int

employee_id is the primary key of this table.

employee_id is also a foreign key that references the Employees table.

Each row indicates that the employee with employee_id is working on project project_id with a workload.

Table: Employees
Column Name	Type
employee_id	int
name	varchar
team	varchar

employee_id is the primary key of this table.

Each row contains information about one employee.

Problem

Write a SQL query to find the employees who are allocated to projects with a workload that exceeds the average workload of all employees in their respective teams.

Return the result table ordered by employee_id, then project_id in ascending order.

Result Format

Your output should have the following columns:

Column Name
employee_id
project_id
employee_name
project_workload
Example
Input

Project table:

project_id	employee_id	workload
1	1	45
1	2	90
2	3	12
2	4	68

Employees table:

employee_id	name	team
1	Khaled	A
2	Ali	B
3	John	B
4	Doe	A
Output
employee_id	project_id	employee_name	project_workload
2	1	Ali	90
4	2	Doe	68

Solution 1
===========
WITH team_avg AS (
    SELECT
        e.team,
        AVG(p.workload) AS avg_workload
    FROM Project p
    JOIN Employees e
        ON p.employee_id = e.employee_id
    GROUP BY e.team
)
SELECT
    p.employee_id,
    p.project_id,
    e.name AS employee_name,
    p.workload AS project_workload
FROM Project p
JOIN Employees e
    ON p.employee_id = e.employee_id
JOIN team_avg t
    ON e.team = t.team
WHERE p.workload > t.avg_workload
ORDER BY p.employee_id, p.project_id;

Solution 2
===========
SELECT
    p.employee_id,
    p.project_id,
    e.name AS employee_name,
    p.workload AS project_workload
FROM Project p
JOIN Employees e
  ON p.employee_id = e.employee_id
WHERE p.workload > AVG(p.workload) OVER (PARTITION BY e.team)
ORDER BY p.employee_id, p.project_id;

Solution 3
===========
SELECT
    p.employee_id,
    p.project_id,
    e.name AS employee_name,
    p.workload AS project_workload
FROM Project p
JOIN Employees e
  ON p.employee_id = e.employee_id
WHERE p.workload > (
    SELECT AVG(p2.workload)
    FROM Project p2
    JOIN Employees e2
      ON p2.employee_id = e2.employee_id
    WHERE e2.team = e.team
)
ORDER BY p.employee_id, p.project_id;
